.TH AISHA 1 "November 2026" "aisha 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aisha \- ai$ha (ai shell hybrid alpha), a shell you can talk to
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aisha
.br
.B aisha
.I request-or-command
.br
.B aisha \-n
.I request
.br
.B aisha \-c
.I line
.br
.B aisha
.I script.sh
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B aisha \-\-lines
.RI < file
.br
.B aisha \-\-setup
.RB [ 0.5b | 1.5b | 3b ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B aisha \-\-setup remove
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aisha
is an interactive shell that accepts both bash and plain-language requests.
Real commands (a program on PATH with flags, paths, pipes or redirects) run in
bash unchanged.
Other lines go to a deterministic rule engine that builds the command from the
words and prints what it understood on a line starting with \(->.
Only when the rules are not confident is a small local language model asked,
through any OpenAI-compatible server; its command is always shown and
confirmed before it runs, and approved answers are remembered.
.PP
It is also a regular shell:
.BR cd ,
.BR export ,
aliases and functions persist between lines; Ctrl-Z,
.BR jobs ,
.BR fg ,
.B bg
and
.I "cmd &"
work; Tab completes commands and paths.
.B "aisha \-c"
and scripts run in plain bash, so aisha can be a login shell.
.PP
Questions such as "how do I delete empty folders" print the command without
running it.
.PP
Commands that delete or change data always ask
.B [y/N]
first, and deletes list the matching files before asking.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
find recursively files older than 2 months from this folder
find logs older than 2 months and move them to archive
edit logs.txt
edit logs.txt with micro
show the 5 newest files here
which files mention "invoice"
what's eating my disk
show file tree
what time is it in tokyo
check for updates
switch to branch dev
delete everything except report.pdf
reboot nginx
reboot in 5 minutes
what can you do
.fi
.SH INSIDE THE SHELL
.TP
.BI ! command
run in bash, skipping the rules
.TP
.BI ? request
skip the rules and ask the LLM
.TP
.BI explain " request"
show what would run, run nothing
.TP
.BR learned ", " forget " \fIrequest\fR"
list or drop remembered LLM answers
.TP
.B llm
check the local model
.TP
.BR exit ", Ctrl-D"
leave
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
print the command that would run, and run nothing
.TP
.BI \-c " line"
like
.BR "bash \-c" :
real commands go straight to bash, plain words are interpreted
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-login
load the login environment (/etc/profile, ~/.profile)
.TP
.B \-\-lines
read plain-language lines from standard input, one at a time
.TP
.B \-\-setup
set up the optional local model: reuses a running server, Ollama or
.B llama-server
on PATH, otherwise downloads llama.cpp and a Qwen2.5-Coder model
(0.5b, 1.5b or 3b) into ~/.local/share/aisha.
.B \-\-yes
answers yes to the download questions;
.B remove
deletes the downloads
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM_URL
OpenAI-compatible endpoint (default http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1, Ollama)
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM_MODEL
model name (default qwen2.5-coder:1.5b)
.TP
.B AISHA_LLM
set to off to disable the LLM fallback
.TP
.B AISHA_THRESHOLD
confidence below which the rules defer to the LLM (default 0.7)
.TP
.B AISHA_CONFIRM
llm (default), always, or destructive
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
editor used by "edit FILE" (through sensible-editor on Debian)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aisha/config.json
settings (same keys as the environment variables, lower case without AISHA_)
.TP
.I ~/.config/aisha/aisharc
bash aliases, functions and exports loaded at start (as is ~/.bash_aliases)
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/aisha
downloaded llama.cpp runtime and model
.TP
.I ~/.config/aisha/learned.json
remembered phrases
.TP
.I ~/.config/aisha/history
command history
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR sensible-editor (1)
